p('Four utilities, one payment plan','title');p('Private capstone research | 7 November 2026 | No default change','small')
p('Your confirmed payment amount is $250,000 per month. This comparison leads with 12 modeled monthly payments, $3M total. The due weeks approximate a calendar schedule. The research balance sheet remains $100M with 10% unsold property and zero rent/cash rate; this is not a fully calibrated personal plan.')
p('Result: no utility winner established','h');p('On the same paths and checks, all four utilities select a 25% candidate / 75% cash-plus-fixed-property anchor blend and pass the independent final all-risk judge under both fixed scenario laws. Raw portfolios fail the separate path-loss check. In this bounded study the hard constraints and validation grid mostly dominate the utility choice. The default stays CARA.')
p('Definitions and what they miss','h');table([['Preference','Argument / definition','Parameter and limitation'],['CARA surplus','u(X)=-exp(-X/T)','T=$10M. Constant dollar risk tolerance; no special aversion increase as surplus nears zero.'],['CRRA gross','u(G)=(G/W0)^(1-g)/(1-g)','g=10. Relative aversion on gross marked wealth; payments affect constraints, not this objective. G must be positive.'],['HARA payment floor','u(G)=((G-L)/S0)^(1-g)/(1-g)','S0=W0-L; g=S0/T=9.7 for the confirmed plan. Matches local dollar aversion at initial wealth. Undefined at/below floor.'],['Kinked shortfall','u(X)=X/W0-4*max(-X/W0,0)','Below target the marginal penalty is 5x the upside slope. Risk-neutral above target; not a payment-probability guarantee.']],[100,177,198])
p('G is terminal marked wealth, L the terminal cash value of scheduled payments, X=G-L. For g=1, power utility becomes log. HARA(G,L,g) is CRRA(X,g), up to positive scaling. If CRRA already means power utility on NET wealth with the same g, it is not a different alternative. Putting the liability floor on X again would count payments twice.','small')
